## Why This Is Asked

Assesses planning, risk management, data integrity, and cross-team governance for a major migration; tests ability to define milestones, ownership, and metrics beyond high-level talk.

## Key Concepts

- Migration strategy and data integrity checks
- Downtime avoidance and phased rollout (canaries, dual-write)
- Rollback criteria, SLAs, and incident readiness
- Cross-team governance and staffing plans
- Metrics dashboards and validation artifacts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Basic idempotent migration hook (illustrative)
async function migrateBatch(batch) {
  for (const record of batch) {
    try {
      await writeToNewPlatform(record);
      await markAsMigrated(record.id);
    } catch (error) {
      await logMigrationError(record.id, error);
      // Continue processing other records
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests balance governance with velocity, showing the ability to scale contract testing, versioning, and regional rollout while minimizing outages. It probes tooling choices and how to communicate contracts across teams.

## Key Concepts

- Contract-first API design
- OpenAPI catalog
- Pact consumer-driven contracts
- CI/CD contract gates
- Deprecation/migration strategy
- Multi-region rollout and versioning

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenAPI-like contract snippet (simplified)
const openapiSpec = {
  openapi: "3.0.0",
  info: { title: "Shared API", version: "1.0.0" },
  paths: {
    "/messages": {
      get: { responses: { "200": { description: "OK" } } }
    }
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a breaking change in production when a consumer is not updated?
- What metrics would you track to decide when to deprecate an endpoint?
